# FIXED, DEFECT 2143, 2026-10-25, M-rechecked-issues (its other half; the
# issue's swapped shape, with a third unit).
#
# SYMPTOM: of a program whose root and two modules each bind a name their
# header refuses, the seed's compiler (`sources 5f45d6514b22d650`) told one
# unit's mistake per build, in the order the units compiled: `K_GONE`
# alone at exit 1, then `narrow` of `fixedbugs2143/wide` once `K_GONE` was
# gone, then `K_NONE` of `fixedbugs2143/vals` once `narrow` took an `i32`.
#
# CAUSE: a round's verdict was its first refused unit's, and the other
# units' refusals were kept for the tag round alone (`cli/assemble.hero`'s
# `per_module`).
#
# FIX: every refused unit is read for whose its refusal is, each under its
# own module's headers, and every mistake is told in the one build, the
# units in their order (`cli/refused_units.hero`); `K_DIV`, a value only the
# probe sees, follows them.
use fixedbugs2143/wide
use fixedbugs2143/vals

extern "fixedbugs-2128-values.h"
    constant K_GONE: i64  #~ ffi_unknown_name

function main()
    print(K_GONE + wide.got() + vals.got())
